WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en-US

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:03.570
If you're operating an e-commerce
store, then at some point, you'll

00:00:03.570 --> 00:00:07.110
have to figure out how to package,
ship and fulfill your orders.

00:00:07.560 --> 00:00:10.800
Product packaging is the
most direct touchpoint

00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:11.640
with your customer.

00:00:12.120 --> 00:00:14.160
It also happens to be
one of the most underused

00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:15.450
marketing opportunities.

00:00:15.750 --> 00:00:19.230
Great e-commerce packaging isn't
just about protecting your products

00:00:19.230 --> 00:00:20.490
during the shipping process.

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:23.970
It's about creating a memorable
moment for your customers.

00:00:30.090 --> 00:00:33.000
Although the functional aspect
of product packaging is still

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:37.080
important, innovative brands are
beginning to use the unboxing

00:00:37.080 --> 00:00:40.800
experience to win the hearts
of consumers, generate social

00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:43.800
media buzz and differentiate
themselves in the marketplace.

00:00:44.120 --> 00:00:45.910
Today, I'm going to
help you do the same.

00:00:46.240 --> 00:00:49.510
In this video, I'll show
you how top brands designed

00:00:49.510 --> 00:00:53.710
memorable unboxing experiences
to generate repeat purchases

00:00:53.770 --> 00:00:55.390
and attract new customers.

00:00:55.720 --> 00:00:58.540
Make sure to stick around until
the end, because I'll share a free,

00:00:58.720 --> 00:01:02.980
comprehensive guide that will walk
you step-by-step through the entire

00:01:02.980 --> 00:01:04.780
shipping and fulfillment process.

00:01:05.890 --> 00:01:08.100
So what is product packaging?

00:01:08.670 --> 00:01:12.630
Product packaging is so much
more than just a container or

00:01:12.630 --> 00:01:15.330
materials use to protect an item.

00:01:15.690 --> 00:01:18.240
It's your brand's first
impression to customers.

00:01:18.600 --> 00:01:20.580
It should provide
value and excitement.

00:01:20.910 --> 00:01:23.789
It should make your customers
eager to share the experience.

00:01:24.060 --> 00:01:27.539
When we think of product packaging
in this way, it causes us to

00:01:27.539 --> 00:01:30.800
consider the potential touch points
that we'll have with our customer.

00:01:31.214 --> 00:01:33.554
From the moment the product
leaves our facility until it

00:01:33.554 --> 00:01:34.964
arrives in the customer's hands.

00:01:35.835 --> 00:01:38.024
Why is product packaging important?

00:01:38.445 --> 00:01:42.044
As you might imagine, having a
physical store can provide ample

00:01:42.044 --> 00:01:45.285
opportunities for interaction
with customers as they can see

00:01:45.285 --> 00:01:48.930
the smile on your face, have a
conversation with you and even

00:01:48.930 --> 00:01:52.020
hear your polite tone of voice
as you hand them their products.

00:01:52.380 --> 00:01:55.080
With online retailers,
this is not the case.

00:01:55.290 --> 00:01:59.460
So the goal of e-commerce packaging
is to establish a similar warm

00:01:59.490 --> 00:02:02.610
feeling when customers receive
and open their packages.

00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:05.760
This is what makes product
packaging so important for

00:02:05.760 --> 00:02:08.550
any brand looking to better
connect with their consumers,

00:02:08.729 --> 00:02:10.500
especially in a crowded market.

00:02:11.489 --> 00:02:15.540
A recent survey from dotcom
distribution found that 40% of

00:02:15.540 --> 00:02:19.619
consumers are likely to make
repeat purchases from an online

00:02:19.619 --> 00:02:21.630
merchant with premium packaging.

00:02:21.899 --> 00:02:25.079
The same study also found that
premium packaging makes a brand

00:02:25.079 --> 00:02:28.760
feel upscale as well as builds
anticipation for delivery.

00:02:29.130 --> 00:02:32.460
Many brands are realizing that
packaging presents a great

00:02:32.460 --> 00:02:36.000
opportunity to elaborate on key
messaging or strengthen their

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:40.380
brand identity and even compel
customers to spread awareness on

00:02:40.380 --> 00:02:42.540
several social media platforms.

00:02:42.765 --> 00:02:45.855
If it looks good, feels
good, sounds good, or stands

00:02:45.855 --> 00:02:49.065
for something meaningful,
customers will have no problem

00:02:49.095 --> 00:02:50.625
letting others know about it.

00:02:50.955 --> 00:02:54.615
See your product packaging as
an extension of your brand.

00:02:54.795 --> 00:02:58.365
When I started my tea shop,
we became very well known for

00:02:58.365 --> 00:03:02.205
displaying a high level of
customer service, as stated by

00:03:02.205 --> 00:03:05.745
hundreds of customers across
various review sites like Google

00:03:05.745 --> 00:03:07.834
reviews, TripAdvisor and Yelp.

00:03:08.364 --> 00:03:11.645
Many of these reviews stemmed
from the day-to-day shenanigans

00:03:11.765 --> 00:03:14.255
that we would perform when
customers walked into our store.

00:03:14.675 --> 00:03:17.945
We would randomly dress up
in Disney costumes, handout

00:03:17.945 --> 00:03:21.365
chocolates, and surprise customers
with gifts on their birthday,

00:03:21.515 --> 00:03:25.685
leaving them in disbelief and in
anticipation for their next visit.

00:03:26.135 --> 00:03:29.385
Once we launched our online
shop, we knew there would be high

00:03:29.385 --> 00:03:32.775
expectations for us to upkeep
this level of service and still

00:03:32.775 --> 00:03:36.315
incorporate the wow factor that
our customers had come to enjoy.

00:03:36.615 --> 00:03:39.645
With this in mind, we made
it our duty to ensure that

00:03:39.675 --> 00:03:42.525
every customer that placed
an order for the first time

00:03:42.765 --> 00:03:45.355
received a personal handwritten
letter from the founders.

00:03:45.965 --> 00:03:49.120
Every order received three
free samples and other branded

00:03:49.120 --> 00:03:52.000
material inside their polka
dot ribbon box filled with

00:03:52.000 --> 00:03:53.620
sparkly tissue and confetti.

00:03:54.070 --> 00:03:56.290
Our goal was to capture
the key elements of our

00:03:56.290 --> 00:03:59.440
brand and share it with our
customers all over the world.

00:03:59.560 --> 00:04:02.830
The geek and gaming merchant
subscription box service Loot

00:04:02.830 --> 00:04:06.170
Crate is a great example of a
brand that is delighting their

00:04:06.170 --> 00:04:09.890
customers with every aspect of
the product packaging experience.

00:04:10.220 --> 00:04:13.640
Every month they send their
subscribers a theme tailored box

00:04:13.640 --> 00:04:17.690
of surprises, such as their Harry
Potter box or chamber of secrets.

00:04:17.870 --> 00:04:21.170
These boxes have everything
from Hogwarts inspired letters,

00:04:21.260 --> 00:04:24.560
explaining the contents of the
package to Phoenix badges and

00:04:24.560 --> 00:04:28.820
posters, everything that would
leave a subscriber anticipating

00:04:28.850 --> 00:04:30.560
their next monthly package.

00:04:30.740 --> 00:04:34.080
The real value add with a
company like Loot Crate, goes

00:04:34.080 --> 00:04:37.800
beyond the box and what's inside
as they go above and beyond

00:04:37.800 --> 00:04:41.130
for their subscribers by also
giving them a sneak peek at

00:04:41.130 --> 00:04:44.820
their behind the scenes videos
via the looters mobile app.

00:04:45.150 --> 00:04:48.120
In this case, you can see that
Loot crate understands that

00:04:48.120 --> 00:04:51.870
the term product packaging
is everything from the box to

00:04:51.870 --> 00:04:54.060
the contents, to mobile app.

00:04:54.300 --> 00:04:56.010
It's an all-inclusive package.

00:04:56.460 --> 00:05:00.945
And then there was apple, if
you've ever purchased anything

00:05:01.485 --> 00:05:03.885
from Apple, then you know
how much detail they put into

00:05:03.885 --> 00:05:07.695
every aspect of the product
packaging, the sleek minimalistic

00:05:07.695 --> 00:05:11.055
box, the glossy overlay, the
product placement in the box.

00:05:11.865 --> 00:05:14.235
Even the Mac charger comes
beautifully, wound up and

00:05:14.235 --> 00:05:15.705
looks aesthetically pleasing.

00:05:16.155 --> 00:05:19.335
The tiny branded booklet is
the icing on the cake, as it

00:05:19.425 --> 00:05:23.595
educates on all aspects of the
product you just purchased while

00:05:23.595 --> 00:05:26.655
also making you feel as if you
just joined an elite sorority

00:05:26.655 --> 00:05:28.575
club of tech users globally.

00:05:29.025 --> 00:05:32.595
Apple has and continues to
deliver awesome experiences

00:05:32.595 --> 00:05:33.855
with their product packaging.

00:05:34.875 --> 00:05:38.235
Next up we'll discuss types
of packaging and their uses.

00:05:38.625 --> 00:05:42.045
Great packaging should be
just as functional as it is

00:05:42.045 --> 00:05:45.645
beautiful because customers are
depending on us to ship their

00:05:45.645 --> 00:05:48.045
products efficiently and safely.

00:05:48.465 --> 00:05:51.885
So let's take a look at the most
commonly used packaging and what

00:05:51.885 --> 00:05:54.915
they're used for so that you
can get a better idea of what

00:05:54.915 --> 00:05:57.885
type of packaging works best
for you and your business needs.

00:05:58.515 --> 00:06:02.849
Corrugated boxes, padded
mail, bags and envelopes,

00:06:03.120 --> 00:06:04.650
custom product packaging.

00:06:05.025 --> 00:06:06.015
Let's break these down.

00:06:06.945 --> 00:06:08.115
Corrugated boxes.

00:06:08.235 --> 00:06:10.844
These are the most widely
used product packaging by

00:06:10.844 --> 00:06:14.565
retailers as they're simple
sturdy, and don't add too

00:06:14.565 --> 00:06:16.065
much weight to your shipment.

00:06:16.395 --> 00:06:19.455
The fact that corrugated
boxes can be recycled also

00:06:19.455 --> 00:06:22.500
makes them an eco-friendly
option that your customers

00:06:22.500 --> 00:06:23.700
will definitely appreciate.

00:06:23.970 --> 00:06:27.690
If your products are a bit heavier
than normal, these boxes also have

00:06:27.720 --> 00:06:31.530
double-walled options to provide
extra strength and durability.

00:06:32.220 --> 00:06:33.180
Padded mailers.

00:06:33.300 --> 00:06:36.780
These packages are often used
for shipping smaller or flat

00:06:36.780 --> 00:06:40.890
items, such as books, handcrafted
items, or even jewelry.

00:06:41.160 --> 00:06:44.610
The bonus with these packages
is that they're lined with a

00:06:44.610 --> 00:06:46.410
bubble padding to keep the items.

00:06:47.315 --> 00:06:50.555
One drawback with padded mailers
would be the fact that they're

00:06:50.555 --> 00:06:51.875
not the most eco-friendly.

00:06:52.650 --> 00:06:55.140
And this may cause some
concern for your customers.

00:06:55.170 --> 00:06:56.160
So keep this in mind.

00:06:57.150 --> 00:06:58.500
Bags and envelopes.

00:06:58.650 --> 00:07:01.530
Consider using this option
if you're shipping items that

00:07:01.530 --> 00:07:03.300
are light, but not fragile.

00:07:03.690 --> 00:07:07.530
Bags and envelopes are very
strong, durable, and typically

00:07:07.530 --> 00:07:11.310
self-sealing, which does make it
easy to package orders, adding

00:07:11.310 --> 00:07:14.640
your logo or branded message
to these bags or envelopes is

00:07:14.640 --> 00:07:17.935
an easy way to strengthen your
brand identity and give your

00:07:17.935 --> 00:07:19.315
customer something special.

00:07:19.885 --> 00:07:23.664
Companies like Hero Packaging can
help you create branded packages

00:07:23.755 --> 00:07:25.435
with zero waste alternatives.

00:07:25.525 --> 00:07:26.815
So consider checking them out.

00:07:27.835 --> 00:07:29.005
Custom packaging.

00:07:29.395 --> 00:07:33.054
This option is where you can really
get your creative juices flowing.

00:07:33.474 --> 00:07:37.525
Custom packaging can include
everything from die-cut boxes to

00:07:37.525 --> 00:07:41.945
branded ribbons wrapping and the
objective with custom packaging

00:07:41.945 --> 00:07:45.724
is to fully immerse your customer
into your brand and allow them

00:07:45.724 --> 00:07:48.515
to feel like they just ordered
a piece of your brand identity.

00:07:48.965 --> 00:07:52.085
If done right customers won't
waste any time, pulling out

00:07:52.085 --> 00:07:54.905
their smartphone and taking
pictures and videos while

00:07:54.905 --> 00:07:56.164
unboxing their package.

00:07:56.434 --> 00:07:59.075
If you need some inspiration
to help kickstart your idea,

00:07:59.775 --> 00:08:01.575
check out East Coast packaging.

00:08:01.805 --> 00:08:04.784
They are a very popular choice when
it comes to customized packaging

00:08:04.784 --> 00:08:09.465
materials, such as bubble mailers,
package cushioning, and a lot more.

00:08:09.825 --> 00:08:13.635
They also offer over 1300
sizes of boxes, so there's

00:08:13.635 --> 00:08:14.625
plenty to choose from.

00:08:14.955 --> 00:08:18.525
You can also explore apps like
ARKA on the Shopify app store

00:08:18.645 --> 00:08:22.485
who also offer amazing selections
for all your packaging needs.

